id: pm-memory-wvy5
title: Time-bounded standing guidance with renewal evidence
description: "Model truth validity independently of task deadlines, reusing standing pins, recency ranking and verification."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:59:39.556Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T21:25:02.813Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Expired guidance is labeled or excluded according to explicit recall policy; concurrent renewals preserve every evidence record and native history; frozen-clock fixture is deterministic; typed SDK and CLI work without git; compact JSON and TOON; targeted tests and CI npm plus Bun release gates; read-only public tracker validation with measured counts.
parent: pm-memory-0kwy
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:59:46.676Z",codex-agent,"Design: attach evidence-backed validity windows to existing pinned Knowledge items using registered metadata and the process writer lock. Append each renewal; preserve native history. Default recall/index exclude expired, scheduled or content-changed guidance; explicit label policy returns state and bounds. Existing unbounded guidance stays compatible. Verify remains independent: file evidence cannot silently renew policy. CLI and SDK require no git."
  "2026-10-21T22:03:13.694Z",codex-agent,"Targeted six-test run passed, including independent-process renewals and no-git CLI JSON/TOON output. New guidance module measured 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. Added export refusal to avoid silently stripping validity in portable harness formats; separate portable-round-trip follow-up created. Full release evidence will run in CI only because the host is saturated."
  "2026-10-21T22:06:09.868Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public tracker validation: semantic-recall commit 72636194fc18e4c79a0a253e47a3d6c60cf27f69; 10 complete items, 2 nonempty bodies, 133150 input JSON bytes, 26 source hashes unchanged. Real text projected in memory with synthetic windows: current 3, expired 3, scheduled 2, needs-renewal 2. Exclude emitted 3 at 209 tokens; label emitted all 10 at 800 tokens; zero budget omissions. Non-git read-only source with no git executable. Full methodology and limits in docs/time-bounded-guidance-validation.md."
  "2026-10-21T22:06:54.947Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only eligibleGuidance with the pre-feature pass-through behavior made the frozen-clock regression fail (1 failed, expired/scheduled advice leaked). Separately removing only the renewal persistence mutation made the independent-process regression fail (1 failed, revisions [1,1] instead of [1,2]). Restored both functions. Previous restored combined run: 10 passed; guidance module 100/100/100/100. Current CLI 2026.10.21 overlap rechecked: deadline scheduling and context deadline pressure do not model guidance validity."
  "2026-10-21T22:09:14.201Z",codex-agent,"Tracker-linked regression command passed 6/6 after both behavioral reverts were restored. Final review added a consolidation preflight refusal: merging bounded guidance into another memory could otherwise widen expired policy into unbounded advice. The new regression checks both bounded source and bounded target and verifies no writes on refusal. Local default health sees a global pm-github host-version skew (pinned CLI 2026.10.19 versus extension built for 2026.10.21); isolated CI identity is checked separately without changing package pins or host extensions."
  "2026-10-21T22:09:35.535Z",codex-agent,"Consolidation guard regression passed 1/1; removing only its new preflight refusal made that regression fail 1/1 (missing expected rejection), then restored. Isolated health passed strict exit with all 10 checks acceptable; the inherited pending telemetry queue is advisory. Final local typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication gate passed at unchanged thresholds. Tracker-linked tests passed 6/6, and combined validity/CLI tests passed 10/10 before the additional consolidation regression."
  "2026-10-21T22:14:26.404Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/8 is ready for review, based on main and explicitly dependent on #5 merging first. Implementation commit a410421a48bce2116027bf663ab9447f745a0a60 passed CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/39684481942: npm release steps on Node 22 and 26 each passed 207 tests; bun run release:check on Node 26 passed another 207. Every coverage run measured all 23 source files at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines, with zero failures/skips. Packed npm/Bun acceptance passed 2 tests in each of the three gate contexts. No merge or release. Automated reviewer skips, quotas and neutral statuses are missing review evidence, not approval. Portable windows remain follow-up pm-memory-1363; direct external writers and hosted deployment remain documented boundaries. Releasing the implementation claim for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-21T22:15:12.731Z",codex-agent,Final SDK review found that the compact retrieval description also carries semantic advice and must be included in the evidence digest. Extending the digest and content-edit regression to cover native description edits before final handoff; full final-head CI will be required again.
  "2026-10-21T22:16:11.892Z",codex-agent,"Description evidence binding: targeted content-edit regression passed 1/1 with the updated digest. Reverting only guidanceHash to omit description made that regression fail 1/1 (changed retrieval advice was still eligible), then restored. Typecheck, lint and zero duplication passed again. Existing full CI receipt remains recorded for the prior implementation; the final exact-head CI run and counts will be linked in PR #8 after this correction. No additional local full gate was run. Releasing the claim for final CI and orchestrator verification; retain in-progress status."
  "2026-10-22T21:15:58.548Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator requested updating stacked PR 8 onto validated semantic head 7c44dc746415d7ac2720fecb6aab9efa80e827ab. Pulled the clean remote head first. Ancestry confirms this branch depends directly on semantic recall and is independent of outcome utility. Merge origin/main first, then semantic recall, retaining expiry rechecks, validity policy/labels and renewal evidence alongside automatic lexical fallback, partial-evidence notes, provenance and cache diagnostics. Validate both parent behaviors and full npm/Bun gates; preserve histories and keep this feature in progress."
  "2026-10-22T21:24:54.619Z",codex-agent,"Merged origin/main first, then semantic head 7c44dc746415d7ac2720fecb6aab9efa80e827ab directly; this feature remains independent of outcome utility. Regenerated changelog and resolved recall/type conflicts by retaining commit-time expiry filtering, validity bounds/status, source provenance and the validity policy argument on every recall path, including the new locked auto fallback. Added a real non-git frozen-clock regression that forces five content conflicts as standing guidance expires, then requires labelled lexical fallback to retain both rows, the expired label/bounds, source and emitted-only counters. Combined expiry-recheck, labelled-fallback, rejected-length, auto-conflict and provenance checks pass 5/5; typecheck, zero duplication, npm ci and strict tracker health pass, with no pending receipts."
  "2026-10-22T21:25:02.809Z",codex-agent,"Four independent parent-side behavioral revert proofs retain the new test: restoring only commitRecall from semantic parent 7c44dc7 makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^stacked auto fallback\" test/guidance.test.ts fail 0/1 (missing validity metadata); restoring only commitRecall from validity parent 738880b fails 0/1 (missing source); restoring only recall from semantic parent fails 0/1 (lost labelled inclusion after expiry because the validity policy is absent); restoring only recall from validity parent fails 0/1 (conflict instead of automatic lexical fallback). Each exit is 1 for the intended regression; every artifact was restored immediately. The combined functions then pass the same regression 1/1. Source imports need no dist rebuild. Full npm and Bun gates will run in CI at unchanged thresholds; the local shared-host timing exception is documented on semantic PR 5."
